index bacd896..73a4550 100644
--- a/docs/rowhouse-atlas-method.md
+++ b/docs/rowhouse-atlas-method.md
@@ -105,3 +105,16 @@ A nomination-grade or regulatory atlas needs one polygon per surviving building,
 age band, alteration and condition, current use, occupancy/tenure where ethically collectable, linked archival
 photographs, and an audit trail for every change. Satellite and machine classification can propose candidates;
 street-level inspection, archival evidence and community review must confirm them.
+
+## Scholarship that sits on the map
+
+The explorer directory is not the literature. Working paper 02 — *The row is the city* — lives at
+`/rowhouses/bible` (long form: `/rowhouses/bible/paper.html`; recovered thesis catalog:
+`/rowhouses/bible/theses.html` and `catalog.json`). It keeps four inventories separate:
+
+- Onsawangchai & Funo 2004: **1,656** remaining Rattanakosin units (2001–02 field survey)
+- Crown Property Bureau: **1,960** units across 15 commercial sites
+- Corridor published counts from several papers (Tha Tien 490, Sam Phraeng 119, Bowonniwet 46, Khao Hong 9, Asdang–Ban Mo 108, Srasong–Longtha 98, Luenrit ~220). These are **not** one survey and must not be added into a city total.
+- Overture 2026-07-22.0 review queue: **2,311** shapes, **1,001** strong morphology — not heritage designations
+
+The 1988 composition study (14,421 units) calibrates candidate shape only.
